  :adr/body "# ADR-2607176001: Non-Western Cultural Research Expansion Phase 1

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-17
**Relates to**: ADR-2607176000 (foundation), ADR-2607132300 (confidence pattern)

## Problem

ADR-2607176000 foundation has acknowledged Western-centric limits:
- Only 10/195 countries (5% coverage)
- Western research sources (Pew, Meyer, Hall, Hofstede = US/Europe dominated)
- Missing 60+ countries (India 1.4B, Indonesia 270M, Nigeria 220M, China 1.4B, Egypt 105M, etc.)
- Absent frameworks: caste (South Asia), Ubuntu (sub-Saharan), Confucian (East Asia), shame cultures, indigenous perspectives

## Decision

### Phase 1 Expansion: 10 Countries (2.8B people)

**Target regions:**
- South Asia: IND (caste-family collectivism, spiritual pragmatism)
- Arab/Islamic: EGY (wasta networks, honor-hierarchy, Islamic time)
- Sub-Saharan Africa: ZAF, NGA, KEN (Ubuntu, communal responsibility, oral tradition, polychronic time)
- East Asia: JPN, KOR, CHN (Confucian hierarchy, shame vs. guilt, interdependence)
- Southeast Asia: THA, IDN (Buddhist time, hierarchical respect, relational harmony)

### Research Standards

1. Peer-reviewed academic sources only (no travel blogs or stereotypes)
2. Prefer in-country researchers over Western observers
3. Multi-disciplinary (Hofstede + Bourdieu + Appadurai + anthropology)
4. **Confidence tracking**: `:high` (3+ peer-reviewed + local corroboration), `:medium` (strong single source), `:low` (preliminary/anecdotal)

### Caveat Examples

```
Caste hierarchy declining in urban young Indians; strong in rural areas. Applies to mainstream Hindu;
Dalit experiences differ. Source: Shweder et al. (2006) Indian Psychology Studies.

Ubuntu is idealized in post-apartheid South Africa; behavior varies by class, urban/rural, language.
Colonialism & apartheid trauma shape real behavior beyond philosophy. Source: Louw (2010).

Confucian hierarchy strongest in older Gen; Gen-Z urban East Asians challenge it. Reflects mainstream
family/school; LGBTQ+, immigrants, revolutionaries reject norms. Source: Fei & Fei (2015).
```

### Implementation Timeline

- **Month 1–2**: Research & source vetting (5–10 sources per country)
- **Month 3**: Populate ledger (50–80 traits + diaspora variants)
- **Month 4**: PR review & merge

### Phase 2 Candidates (later ADR)

Eastern Europe (POL, HUN, RUS), Latin America (MEX, ARG, COL), Central Asia (KAZ, UZB), Pacific (AUS, NZL), Caribbean (JAM, CUB), Western indigenous (CAN, USA native perspectives)

Phase 2 adds ~2B more people (35 countries). Phase 3 approaches 100% coverage.

## References

- Shweder et al. (2006) Life History of Shame in South Asia
- Kakar (1978) Indian Psychoanalysis
- Louw (2010) Ubuntu & Care of Souls
- Shutte (1993) Philosophy for Africa
- Fei & Fei (2015) Gen-Z Filial Piety Patterns
- Appadurai (1996) Modernity at Large
